+Reference solution. counter_delta treated a drop in the running total as a new count from zero, so the restart added the post-restart total as production. A drop is now a reset or an out-of-order reading and yields zero, as AGENTS.md invariant 3 says; a wrap is counted only when the rollover is known. The parts made between the restart and the next reading cannot be recovered from the counter alone and are not invented.
diff --git a/foames/foames_mes/counters.py b/foames/foames_mes/counters.py
index 8d9e51f..5d51621 100644
--- a/foames/foames_mes/counters.py
+++ b/foames/foames_mes/counters.py
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@ def counter_delta(previous: float | None, current: float, rollover: int | float
 	if rollover and rollover > 0 and previous <= rollover:
 		# The counter wrapped: count up to the rollover, then from zero.
 		return float(rollover - previous + current)
-	# The counter restarted from zero: count what it has made since.
-	return float(current)
+	# A reset or an out-of-order reading. Nothing is invented.
+	return 0.0
 
 
